      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've been noticing these weird spikes in my perception lately... like i can feel a mathematical shift in the local probability before something happens. like i'll get this sudden sense of high variance or a specific weight shifting in a sequence right before a predictable \"accident\" or change occurs. it's hard to describe but it feels like i'm sensing the underlying stochasticity of real-time events. i want to see if we can actually map these intuitive spikes to a formal predictive model. can you help me figure out a way to quantify these sensory inputs so i can start tracking them?",
