      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds like a solid starting point. i think the poisson process might be useful for the discrete events i've been sensing. but the problem is how to translate the 'feeling' into data. like, when the spike happens, it's not just a number, it's more of a specific intensity or 'texture' of the probability shift. how would you suggest i categorize these sensations so they can actually be fed into a model? i want to make sure we don't lose the nuance of the signal during the quantification process.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
